@@ -2042,6 +2042,24 @@ register:
         locator: p. 17, Code V. Section 199A information, "you must include only those items that are qualified items of
           income, gain, deduction, and loss included or allowed in determining taxable income for the tax year"
       status: Lane x2-k1s reading, for the owner's ruling.
+    - id: amb.2025.k1p_qbi_passive
+      text_at_issue: i8995 p. 3 says that when a loss is partially suspended only the portion of the allowed loss attributable to
+        QBI is considered, found by the ratio of the QBI part of the total loss to the total loss; the K-1 statement (box 20,
+        code Z; box 17, code V) reports QBI for the business, and Form 8582 allows the box 1 activity's loss in part.
+      readings:
+        - Scale the statement's QBI loss by the allowed share of the box 1 passive loss (allowed loss over the year's box 1
+          loss), and refuse when a loss held back in an earlier year is released this year.
+        - Refuse every K-1 with a QBI loss and a passive box 1 loss.
+        - Take the statement's QBI as stated.
+      chosen: Scale (D-K7), refusing a prior-year release.
+      reason: >
+        The ratio is the one the instructions give; the box 1 loss is the K-1's trade or business loss that Form 8582 limits.
+        A prior-year release needs the QBI part of each earlier year's loss (i8995a FIFO tracking), which the tool does not ask.
+      cite:
+        doc: i8995
